		{
			"advancement": "lepidodendron:pf_adv_book_palaeontinid_fletcheriana",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Initially thought to have been a rather conservative early cicada, noted for its similarities with modern members of this group, Fletcheriana is now understood as the closest relative to the more famous palaeontinids, a group of Jurassic and Cretaceous cicadas known for their large size and their elongated moth-like forewings."
